  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Around And Around** (1 review): The Around and Around is singled out as especially fun [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd94-12-08.neumann.seff.5611.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): audience recording; 18 songs; 155 min; rated 2.43/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Good sound for an audience recording, especially considering the Oakland Coliseum; Reviewer says the recording matches their memories of the night; Audience members stand too close to the microphones, and crowd talking during songs intrudes on the recording [3][4][6]\n- **gd1994-12-08.139122.FOB.Schoeps.Ammons.Zimmer.Noel.t-flac16**: source not stated; 18 songs; 152 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer's first Dead show, attended at age 16 with a ticket bought by a friend, having previously disliked the band [4]\n- Band seemed laidback, looking ahead to winter break after a long year [5]\n- High-energy night where Garcia forgot many lyrics and made up for it by jamming solos extra hard [6]\n- Most of the band played competently, but Garcia seemed to be sleepwalking [7]\n- Jerry sounds more together than at other 1994 shows; the following night was better but had more Garcia blunders [3]\n- Reviewer points to the 21 February 1992 show as a related comparison [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd94-12-08.neumann.seff.5611.sbeok.shnf**: transferred by Jon Seff; source: Audience: Neumann KM140's [1]. Also: Recorded with KM-140 microphones straight to DAT; Transfer ran from DAT master through Tascam CD-RW700 to CD, then WAV, then SHN; Jon Seff ripped, shnTooled and seeded it, tracking it for two 80-minute discs [1]\n- **gd1994-12-08.139122.FOB.Schoeps.Ammons.Zimmer.Noel.t-flac16**: taped by John Ammons & Jeff Zimmer; transferred by John Ammons and Joe Noel; source: flac16/48kHz ; John Ammons & Jeff Zimmer Recording: Schoeps MK4s > Bill Reutelhuber Power Supply > Panasonic SV-255 FOB DFC. Mics in hair; John Ammons [2]",
